{"id":"R0014","access":"READ","decision":"INCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"All E1-E7 criteria satisfied for peer-reviewed IEEE TMC journal article on multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","build up an all-sky autonomous computing (ASAP) system to autonomously conduct","Proposes the ASAP primary system architecture, scheduler, predictor, and compressor."],["E2","PDF",10,"VIII.A Evaluation Setup","ASAP has also been deployed on 5 real-world UAVs","Evaluated on 24 UAV airborne computers and 5 real-world quad-rotor UAVs."],["E3","PDF",2,"I. INTRODUCTION","partitions DL model and data among UAV clusters and within each cluster","Explicitly partitions DNN models across UAV clusters and feature data within clusters for collaborative inference."],["E4","PDF",11,"VIII.B Overall Performance","Table III compares the average inference latency of ASAP","Provides indoor and outdoor hardware experiments measuring latency, overhead, predictor error, and accuracy."],["E5","PDF",1,"First-page footnote","Date of publication 15 July 2024; date of current version","Authoritative publisher online publication date 2024-07-15 is within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) play an essential role in emergency cases","Full 17-page report is written in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"First-page footnote","revised 14 May 2024; accepted 7 July 2024.","Peer-reviewed IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing journal article with full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0024","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"No collaborative DNN/CNN/VLM/LLM inference workload; QADA aggregates raw sensor data pools and models processing only as a fixed scalar delay.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"I. INTRODUCTION","We propose data pool aggregation scheme, QADA, for FEI-SEM systems","Primary research contribution proposing the FEI-SEM system and QADA aggregation algorithm."],["E2","PDF",5,"III. PERFORMANCE EVALUATION","We have 3 cases which utilize UAVs: FANET, Random-FANET and QADA-FANET.","Multi-UAV FANET setting evaluated with 10-30 UAV gateways (Table II)."],["E3","PDF",2,"II. QUALITY AWARE DATA AGGREGATOR (QADA)","makes each edge node decide whether to wait for new data","Checked Sections II (II.A-II.C) and III: QADA only aggregates sensor data pools among neighbor UAVs using VoIU, spatial dispersion, age, and fairness without any DNN model or neural inference workload."],["E3","PDF",3,"II.C Data Aggregation Protocol","waiting for data pool to fill or, forwarding current pool to neighbors","Checked Sections II.C and III (Table II): onboard EI processing is represented only by a constant scalar delay (250 ms) in OMNeT++ simulations with no DNN/CNN/VLM/LLM inference."],["E4","PDF",4,"III. PERFORMANCE EVALUATION","Our evaluation methodology consist of creating detailed OMNET++ simulations with INET framework.","Reports OMNeT++/INET simulation experiments across AoI, throughput, fairness, VoIU, and intelligence quality."],["E5","PDF",1,"First-page footer","Downloaded on April 26,2024 at 08:03:16 UTC from IEEE Xplore.","GLOBECOM 2023 proceedings paper available online on IEEE Xplore on or before 2024-04-26, within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","Smart environmental monitoring is crucial for public health and ecological balance","Full 6-page report is written in English."],["E7","https://gcn.comsoc.org/ieee-global-communications-conference-2023-globecom-2023-8%E2%80%9312-december-2023-kuala-lumpur-malaysia",0,"IEEE ComSoc Conference Report","11,244 reviews were completed for all eligible submissions","Official IEEE ComSoc report confirms peer review for IEEE GLOBECOM 2023 proceedings; PDF provides full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0036","access":"READ","decision":"INCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"All E1-E7 criteria satisfied for peer-reviewed IEEE TCCN journal article jointly orchestrating multi-UAV YOLOv5 edge video inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","we propose the scene-adaptive configuration control","Primary research article proposing the SAC^2 accuracy profiler and configuration control optimizer."],["E2","PDF",11,"VI. PERFORMANCE EVALUATION","We set 100 UAVs randomly distributed in the targeted surveillance area","Evaluates a multi-UAV low-altitude surveillance network scaling up to 100 UAVs."],["E3","PDF",4,"III. SYSTEM DESCRIPTION AND PROBLEM FORMULATION","decides for each UAV whether the following video chunk is necessary","Jointly schedules multi-UAV video-chunk inference requests, frame rate/resolution, shared uplink bandwidth, and edge detection capacity."],["E3","PDF",10,"VI. PERFORMANCE EVALUATION","The edge server runs a YOLOv5 object detection model to generate","Explicit DNN (YOLOv5) object-detection inference workload orchestrated across the multi-UAV-to-edge hierarchy."],["E4","PDF",11,"VI. PERFORMANCE EVALUATION","evaluate scenario generalization by testing the method across diverse surveillance environments","Provides simulation evaluation on the ETH dataset comparing SAC^2 against OPT, FC, CBA, AU, and RU baselines."],["E5","PDF",1,"First-page footnote","Date of publication 8 December 2025; date of current version","Authoritative publisher online publication date 2025-12-08 is within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","Low-altitude uncrewed aerial vehicles (UAVs) are increasingly deployed for urban surveillance","Full 16-page report is written in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"First-page footnote","Received 29 June 2025; revised 16 October 2025; accepted 30 November","Peer-reviewed IEEE Transactions on Cognitive Communications and Networking journal article with full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0080","access":"READ","decision":"INCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"All E1-E7 criteria satisfied for peer-reviewed IEEE VTC2025-Fall conference paper on multi-UAV edge-cloud collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","This paper presents a novel edge-cloud collaborative inference framework for aerial networks","Primary research paper proposing an alternating optimization framework for confidence thresholds and quantization bits."],["E2","PDF",5,"IV.A Experimental Setup","20 UAVs with non-identical data distributions are synthesized","Evaluates a multi-UAV aerial network of 1 to 20 UAVs."],["E3","PDF",2,"II.A System Model","Each UAV independently conducts onboard feature extraction to lightweight raw data samples","Splits DNN inference between onboard UAV feature extraction and cloud-server confidence/raw-data classification under shared bandwidth."],["E3","PDF",5,"IV.A Experimental Setup","Edge-side employed ResNet-18 and ResNet-34 as lightweight backbones.","Explicit collaborative DNN inference using ResNet-18/34 on UAVs and ResNet-101/152 on the cloud server."],["E4","PDF",5,"IV.A Experimental Setup","All experiments are conducted within a simulated edge-cloud collaborative inference framework","Reports CIFAR-10 accuracy and latency evaluations against Raw-Only, Feat-Only, and GSUP baselines."],["E5","https://vtsociety.org/post/announcement/registration-open-vtc2025-fall",0,"IEEE VTS Conference Announcement","Join us in Chengdu: 19-22 October 2025.","VTC2025-Fall took place Oct 19-22, 2025."],["E5","PDF",1,"First-page footer","Downloaded on August 03,2026 at 07:08:10 UTC from IEEE Xplore.","Confirms IEEE Xplore online publication on or before 2026-08-03, within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) are increasingly deployed for real-time intelligent tasks","Full 6-page report is written in English."],["E7","https://events.vtsociety.org/vtc2025-fall/authors/call-for-papers-2/",0,"VTC2025-Fall Call for Papers","Prospective authors are invited to submit 5-page, original, and unpublished full papers.","Official IEEE VTS CFP confirms peer-reviewed full-paper proceedings for VTC2025-Fall; PDF provides full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0096","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Peer-reviewed UbiComp Companion '25 Cloud2Things workshop paper, but lacks collaborative multi-UAV DNN inference (exterior YOLO is single-UAV onboard, interior swarm streams raw thermal images to a GCS CPU without distributed/orchestrated inference, and multi-UAV evaluation tests path planning).","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","We present ARIES, an autonomous post-disaster reconnaissance approach with computational offloading","Primary research contribution presenting the ARIES inspection system."],["E2","PDF",5,"4.2.2 Human Detection from Infrared Images with YOLO","we simulated swarms with 2 to 8 UAVs each.","Evaluates multi-UAV interior swarm exploration with 2 to 8 UAVs (Tables 4-5)."],["E3","PDF",3,"3.1.3 Cracks and Spalls Detection with YOLO","captures RGB images which are processed onboard by an object detection","Checked Sections 3.1-3.3 and 4.1-4.2: exterior crack/spall detection runs standalone YOLO onboard a single DJI Matrice 100 UAV."],["E3","PDF",3,"3.3.2 Human Detection from Infrared Images with YOLO","These images will be shared to the Ground Control Station for processing","Interior Crazyflie swarm only forwards raw thermal images to a single GCS CPU for YOLO12-nano without layer/feature partitioning, fusion, or multi-UAV inference orchestration."],["E3","PDF",6,"5 Conclusion","swarm UAV path generation are offloaded to the Ground Control Station","Offloading separates path planning (GCS) from single-UAV exterior detection; Tables 1 and 3 benchmark standalone YOLO models offline while Tables 4-5 simulate RRT*/A*/Voronoi path planning."],["E4","PDF",4,"4.1.2 Crack and Spall Detection with YOLO","The 15 models were trained for up to 300 epochs.","Provides empirical YOLO benchmarks (Tables 1 and 3) and PyBullet multi-UAV path-planning simulations (Tables 4-5)."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","UbiComp Companion '25, October 12-16, 2025, Espoo, Finland.","Proceedings date October 2025 is wholly within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","We present ARIES a multi-agent single and multi-Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAV) approach","Full 6-page report is written in English."],["E7","https://cloud2things.netsons.org/",0,"Workshop Program and Paper Submission","The review process is single blind. All accepted papers will be published","Official Cloud2Things 2025 (UbiComp/ISWC 2025 workshop) website lists ARIES in the program and confirms single-blind peer review via Microsoft CMT for 6-page ACM proceedings papers."]]}
{"id":"R0105","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"No DNN inference workload; models generic bit-level task offloading and uses PPO solely as the resource-allocation optimizer.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","We formulate the problem as a centralized Markov decision process (MDP)","Primary research paper proposing a PPO and feasibility-allocator resource management method."],["E2","PDF",2,"II.B Network Model","We consider one MEC server and N UAVs","Evaluates a multi-UAV swarm of 2 to 6 UAVs in Fig. 4 (p. 5)."],["E3","PDF",2,"II.B Network Model","amounts of workload processed locally, offloaded to neighboring UAVs via D2D cooperation","Checked Sections II, III, and IV: tasks are generic bit arrivals with scalar cycles/bit and no DNN/CNN/VLM/LLM inference workload."],["E3","PDF",4,"III.B Adaptive Resource Allocation Algorithm for Highly Dynamic Scenarios","Policy parameters are refined through proximal policy optimization using accumulated experience trajectories","Neural network (PPO) is used exclusively as an optimizer for generic bit-level offloading; Section IV evaluates only delay and energy vs task size (MB) and device count."],["E4","PDF",4,"IV. SIMULATION RESULTS AND DISCUSSIONS","We evaluate three schemes under fast-varying channel conditions and stochastic task arrival","Provides simulation evaluation comparing average delay and energy against random and static 20/20/60 baselines."],["E5","PDF",1,"First-page footer","Downloaded on July 07,2026 at 01:13:36 UTC from IEEE Xplore.","IEEE CCPQT 2025 (held Oct 24-26, 2025) paper available online on IEEE Xplore on or before 2026-07-07, within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","The convergence of the internet of things and artificial intelligence is pushing","Full 5-page report is written in English."],["E7","https://www.academicenter.com/conferences/details/IEEE_CCPQT2025.html",0,"Publication Information","论文经过严格同行评议，正式录用的文章将由IEEE出版","Conference page confirms strict peer review and IEEE proceedings publication for CCPQT 2025; PDF contains full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0107","access":"READ","decision":"AWAITING_CLASSIFICATION","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"U","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"Authoritative IEEE Xplore online publication month/day for the assessed IEEE TVT Early Access version (DOI 10.1109/TVT.2026.3733130, copyright 2026, downloaded 2026-11-27) cannot be verified against the 2026-11-26 cutoff.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","this paper proposes UAV-SFGC, a collaborative framework that jointly optimizes multi-UAV semantic","Primary research article proposing the UAV-SFGC framework and JSCR-GRPO algorithm."],["E2","PDF",9,"VI.A Experimental Setup","each UAV is equipped with an NVIDIA Jetson NX module","Evaluates a multi-UAV collaborative network with N=4 UAVs."],["E3","PDF",4,"III.B Collaborative Semantic Representation and Fusion Model","each UAV independently performs semantic inference based on its local multimodal observations","Multiple UAVs run multimodal VLM experts (BLIP/CLIP/TinyBLIP/TinyCLIP), transmit semantic symbols via A2A links, fuse representations via weighted attention, and apply adaptive compression for VQA inference."],["E4","PDF",9,"VI.A Experimental Setup","The experiments are conducted on the COCO-based Visual Question Answering (VQA) dataset","Reports PyTorch simulation results on COCO-based VQA comparing accuracy, QoE, and convergence against single-expert and PPO baselines."],["E5","PDF",1,"Top banner and footer","Citation information: DOI 10.1109/TVT.2026.3733130","PDF is an IEEE TVT Early Access author version showing only copyright year 2026 and no publication month/day; downloaded 2026-11-27 (after the 2026-11-26 cutoff), and public web search found no accessible IEEE Xplore publication date for this assessed version, leaving E5 unresolved."],["E5","PDF",1,"First-page footer","Downloaded on November 27,2026 at 02:37:51 UTC from IEEE Xplore.","Download timestamp is one day after the 2026-11-26 cutoff, so the possible 2026 online publication interval crosses the cutoff."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","Semantic communication is transforming wireless networks by shifting the focus from bit-level","Full 14-page report is written in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"Top banner","This article has been accepted for publication in IEEE Transactions on Vehicular","Accepted peer-reviewed journal article in IEEE Transactions on Vehicular Technology with full text, method, and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0157","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"No collaborative multi-UAV DNN inference; executes standalone on-device ResNet on GAP8 for selective AR video streaming or standalone single-drone image upload to a server running YOLOv5.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","we propose an Energy-Efficient Framework for Video Streaming and Augmented Reality called","Primary research paper proposing the E2AR model-memory and selective AR streaming framework."],["E2","PDF",5,"4.1 Experimental Setup","To evaluate the proposed approach, we used two tiny UAVs, called Crazyflie","Evaluated in a real-world multi-drone scenario with two Crazyflie 2.0 UAVs and a HoloLens 2."],["E3","PDF",4,"3.2 Energy-Efficient Augmented Reality (E2AR)","processes them through the deployed E2 model, and selectively streams video frames","Checked Sections 3.1-3.2 and 4.1-4.2: on-device inference is standalone single-drone ResNet execution on GAP8 to gate video streaming to HoloLens rather than distributed/collaborative DNN inference."],["E3","PDF",6,"4.2 Experimental Results","sending captured images to a server, where the YOLOv5 model performs human","In the two-drone hallway demo, Drone 1 independently uploads raw frames to a server for YOLOv5 while Drone 2 explores opposite rooms; Fig. 6 measures single-GAP8 energy/throughput without multi-drone inference partitioning, fusion, or orchestration."],["E4","PDF",5,"4.2 Experimental Results","On-device experimental results on the GAP8 comparing the baseline and the proposed","Provides GAP8 hardware power, energy, and throughput measurements plus a two-drone HoloLens implementation."],["E5","https://acm-ieee-sec.org/2025/dronesys.php",0,"Important Dates","Workshops Date: December 6, 2025","Official DroneSys 2025 (ACM/IEEE SEC '25) workshop date is Dec 6, 2025 (conference Dec 3-6, 2025), wholly within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","The safety, energy efficiency, and small size of smart drones have led","Full 7-page report is written in English."],["E7","https://acm-ieee-sec.org/2025/dronesys.php",0,"Submission Guidelines and Program","Submissions should omit identifying information to support blind review.","Official DroneSys 2025 workshop website lists E2AR in the program and confirms blind peer review for up to 6-page (excluding references) ACM/IEEE SEC '25 workshop papers."]]}
